RestoreCommittedLogs enabled and no snapshot, NewRaft replays the committed log by pushing one fsmMutateCh message per MaxAppendEntries-sized batch before the FSM goroutine is started; when the committed backlog requires more batches than the queue's 128 slots, the send blocks and NewRaft never returns, so the node never starts.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Config.RestoreCommittedLogs=true with a CommitTrackingLogStore, no snapshot covering the committed range, and a restored commit index whose replay needs more than 128 batches of MaxAppendEntries entries (DefaultConfig sets MaxAppendEntries 64 and TrailingLogs 10240, so about 8192 retained entries; MaxAppendEntries is validated positive and at most 1024, so the boundary scales with the configured value); observed for 8402 entries (132 batches) with a bounded 15 second wait, against 8002 entries (126 batches) returning in 0-3 ms.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_fsm_mutate_buffer\\\",\\\"api_goroutines_after_restore\\\",\\\"raft_processlogs_applybatch\\\",\\\"config_defaults\\\",\\\"config_validation\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"78d56323ae6646da8140c38ebed9bd1c\\\":[7,9]}}\n]\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
